  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Climate Change Resilience and Social Integration of Displaced People in Settlements of Western Belize</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to support displaced persons in migrant settlements in Western Belize to become productive members of their host communities and participate in furthering their common resilience, socio-economic growth, and sustainable development. Indeed, the lack of proper integration of migrants in Western Belize into the Belizean society, lack of basic services, and exposure to the impacts of climate change make them susceptible to continued displacement. As such, this project, jointly run between the International Organization for Migration (IOM) and the Sustainable Development Unit (SDU) of the Government of Belize, seeks to prevent further displacement through integrated service delivery, as well as enhanced prevention, protection, and solutions for disaster and climate-related displacement.</narrative>
  </description>
